# CSE-445 Project

## Project Title
**Multi-Platform Social Sentiment Evolution**

## Project Description
This project aims to collect public social media posts from multiple platforms and analyze how public sentiment and discussion topics change over time. The project will use Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques and clustering algorithms to identify emerging trends and visualize sentiment evolution.

## Objectives
- Collect social media data from multiple platforms.
- Preprocess and clean the collected data.
- Perform sentiment analysis.
- Identify emerging topics using clustering techniques.
- Compare sentiment trends across different platforms.

## Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn
- Jupyter Notebook
- GitHub

## Project Structure
```

CSE-445-Project/
│
├── data/
├── preprocessing/
├── notebooks/
├── docs/
└── README.md

```

## Team Contributions
- Reddit data collection
- Twitter data collection
- Kaggle dataset preprocessing
- Data analysis and clustering

## Current Status
Project initialization and data collection are in progress. The repository will be updated as development continues.
